## Context
`make check` on `origin/main` at `cc3def7` (2026-09-06, after PR #397 merged) is red on
`bench/check_ticket_logs.py`: four log entries are stamped after the commit that
introduced them, which the 2026-09-01 ruling (DECISIONS.md) forbids. None came from
PR #397; all four arrived from sibling sessions today. Per line, the introducing
commit's author time (walked with `git log -S` on the line text, not blame):

| ticket:line | stamped | introduced by | author time |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0029:39 | 10:05Z | `f47ba7f` | 09:52Z |
| 0029:41 | 16:20Z | `b00f500` | 16:00Z |
| 0029:42 | 17:05Z | `c1b7b58` | 16:14Z |
| 0719:8 | 17:10Z | `c1b7b58` | 16:14Z |

Found by the raid on ticket 0714 at its wrap-up `make check` against main. The
same class as the 0714 stamp both PR #395 and #397 corrected: a wall-clock
time typed into the log ahead of the commit that carried it.

## Actions
1. Correct each stamp to the author time of its introducing commit, per the
   ruling's own remedy. No entry text changes.

## Exit criteria
- [x] `python3 bench/check_ticket_logs.py` reports OK (1527 entries across 278 tickets)
